---
title: Instant Pot White and Brown Rice Blend
servings: 6
time required: 1 hour
tags: rice, side-dish, instant-pot, pressure-cooker
description: Equal parts white and brown rice cooked together in one Instant Pot pressure-cook cycle.
---

Rinse the @brown rice{1%cup} and @white rice{1%cup} together under cold water, then drain well. Use the same standard measuring cup for the rice and water, not the Instant Pot cup.

Put both rices and @water{2 1/2%cup} in the #Instant Pot{}. Stir, then lock the lid with the valve set to Sealing. Pressure Cook on High for ~rice{21%minutes}. When the timer ends, leave the pot undisturbed until the pressure releases naturally.

Open the lid and fluff gently. Serve.

> Kitchen-tested: both types of rice go into the pot together. Cook on High pressure for 21 minutes and allow a natural pressure release. Water was increased slightly to 2 1/2 cups for 2 cups total rice.
>
> Source blend — Instant Pot UK’s brown-rice guidance informed the 1.25:1 water ratio and 20-minute High-pressure baseline; Instant Pot Philippines’ guidance informed using manual Pressure Cook timing rather than the white-rice program for brown rice; The Kitchn’s tests informed the caution that rice and appliance results vary. The two-stage timing is my untested adaptation to give the brown rice its longer cook while limiting the white rice’s pressure time. https://instantpot.co.uk/brown-rice/ https://www.instantpot.com.ph/features/ https://www.thekitchn.com/instant-pot-rice-22949278
